Sval: Stop compositing stalls on remote textures from gone canvases

Backport of Mozilla's Bug 2093090 (mozilla-central 340c6c79ba2b,
4d222f0c59ba, d7161e35da77, Firefox 162), unchanged. The first landing
of part 3 was backed out for a gtest build bustage; this takes the
relanded commit. Bug 2093091 builds on this patch.

RemoteTextureMap could not tell an owner that had not registered yet
from one that had already unregistered. A texture that reached the
compositor after its canvas went away was waited on for the full
10 second owner timeout on the compositor thread, which stalls
compositing for every window. Ready checks for an owner that lost its
context, or deferred its unregistration, were also never woken. The fix
remembers which owners live wrappers have seen registered, skips waits
nothing can use, and wakes those ready checks. It adds the gtests in
TestRemoteTextureMap.cpp.

